<title>INDONESIA: Unibank rises on debut.</title>
<headline>Unibank rises on debut.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of newly-listed Indonesian medium-size bank PT United City Bank (Unibank) made strong debut on Friday due to active local-led buying, brokers said.</p>
<p>Unibank opened at 900 rupiah against an offer price of 675 rupiah, but by 0325 GMT had risen to 925 rupiah on a volume of some 16 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Local-led buying boosted Unibank, but further upside is likely to be limited as the rise is already too high,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Unibank floated about 70 million shares, with brokerage firm PT Makindo acting as lead underwriter.  </p>
<p>Unibank said in a public presentation in April that it expected to post a net profit growth of 31.5 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>Unibank posted a net profit of 11.7 billion rupiah in 1996, up 32.8 percent from the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
